  "strategy": "1.Approach and rationale\nThe core idea is to use a multi-start optimization with coordinate-wise updates to escape local minima while maintaining a balance between exploration andexploitation. The algorithm will search in a solution space parameterized by clustered intervals, using a combination of:\n\n- Stochastic coordinate descent for local refinement\n- Hierarchical grid-based initializations to explore diverse solutions\n- Geometric optimization to enforce sum constraints globally\n\nThis differs from the original stochastic search by focusing on structured representations (point clusters) that capture relevant features while reducing dimensionality. The method specifically targets the known plateau region of values around 0.38, using geometric invariance to transfer patterns between resolutions.\n\nKey improvements include:\n- Better local exploration using gradient-free coordinate updates\n- Efficient constraint handling via exponential transformations\n- Dedicated fallback sequences for challenging grids\n- Hierarchical sample reduction to escape local optima\n\nThe main limitation is that grid-based searches may miss theoretically optimal structures, but this heurisitic maintains locality while improving coverage.\n\n2.Mathematical specification\nRepresentation: h(x) = f(x) where f: [0,2] \u2192 [0,1]\nDiscretization: x_i = i * dx for i=0,...,n-1, dx=2/n\nObjective: \n  C\u2085 = max_{k} (1/2) \u222b h(x) (1-h(x+k)) dx\n\u2248 max_{k} [max correlation(h, 1-h)][dx] (discrete form)\n\nConstraints:\n  \u222b_0\u00b2 h(x) = 1\n  0 \u2264 h(x) \u2264 1 everywhere\n\nConstraint formulation:\n  Sum(x) * dx = 1 (with dx=2/n equivalent to sum(x) = n/2)\n  [0,1] bounds per coordinate\n\n3.Implementation procedure\n\n3a. Parameter initialization\n  budget_remaining = budget_s\n  seed = given seed\n  rng = np.random.default_rng(seed)\n  \n  if 'initial_h_values' in globals(): start_point = np.array(initial_h_values)\n  else: start_point = None\n\n  dimension = 720 if start_point is None else len(start_point)\n\n  Define value converters:\n    def to_interval(v): return 0.5 + 0.5*v\n    def from_interval(v): return (v - 0.5)/(0.5)\n\n  Define constraint solver:\n  def project_sum(v):\n      s = np.sum(from_interval(v))\n      # Use exponential screening to minimize penalty\n      sorted_vals = np.sort(np.abs(v))\n      if np.abs(s - target) > tol: raise ValueError(f\"Invalid sum {s} != {target}\")\n\n  Where target = dimension/2 for discrete n-dim grid.\n\n3b. Core optimization loop\n  Create reference grid: points = (i/dimension)*3 for i in range(500) (compressed coarse grid)\n  grid_sizes = [48, 96, 144, 720]\n  best_solution = None\n  best_c5 = float('inf')\n\n  For each (grid_size, scale) in zip(grid_sizes, [1, 0.9, 0.75, 0.5]):\n      if grid_size < dimension and best_solution is not None:\n          candidate = resample(best_solution, dimension, grid_size)   # linear interpolation \n      else:\n          # Generate diversified initialization:\n          candidate = generate_layered_h(10, grid_size)\n          \n      while budget_remaining > min_budget(30, initial=100):\n          # Multi-start with coordinate updates\n          best_hypothesis = None\n          for start_method in ['random', 'gradient']:\n              if start_method=='gradient':\n                  start = stabilize_gradients(candidate)\n              else:\n                  start = perturb_vector(candidate, rng, scale=scale)\n              \n              # Local optimization using coordinate descent\n              local_hypothesis = coordinate_optimize(start)\n              if compute_c5(local_hypothesis) < best_c5:\n                  best_candidate = local_hypothesis\n                  update_acceleration(track)\n\n          if improve_candidate(best_candidate, budget_remaining):\n              update_best(best_candidate)\n              budget_remaining -= refinerate(best_candidate)\n\n 3c. Candidate constraint enforcement\n  def project_clip(v):\n      global_sum = np.sum(np.clip(v, 0, 1))\n      if np.abs(cv - target) > 1e-3:\n          waterfill(v)\n\n 3d. Escaping degenerate solutions\n  def count_saturated(v):\n      s = np.sum(v) / (len(v)/2)\n      return (np.abs(s-1) < tol) or (not any(0<val<1)\n\n  if stuck_indicators > 3 and np.random.rand() < 0.2:\n      candidate = resample(best_solution, dimension, min_grid_size)\n\n4.Search choices and variations\n\n4a. Initialization generators:\n  def generate_layered_h(layers, length):\n      base = np.array([0.5]*length)\n      centers = []\n      num_segments = min(layers, length//2)\n      start_vals = np.linspace(0, 1, num_segments)\n      for s in start_vals:\n          center = rng.integers(0, length-1)\n          centers.append(center)\n          base[center] = s\n      return base\n\n4b. Block adjustment parameters:\n  For grid_size refinement:\n      linear=\"linear\" (stick to best)\n      exponential=\"exponential\" (prioritize improvement)\n\n4c. Constraint handling modes:\n  \"project\" (waterfill)\n  \"image\" (entropic adjustments)\n  \"clip\" (escalate one dimension at a time)\n\n5.Computebudget and robustness\n  Time blocks:\n      Coarsest (48): 10 seconds\n      Medium (96): 100 seconds\n      Next (144): 200 seconds\n      Finest (720): 300 seconds\n\n  Early termination if:\n      (*100) consecutive evaluations show <=1% improvement\n      Absolute time budget would exceed available (stop now)\n\n  Fallback strategy (when stuck):\n      Sample known layer patterns from coarse grids\n      Downward-refined interpolation from best_local+best_global\n\n6.Validation and return contract\n\n  Final validation:\n      Finalize solution by: clip then project to sum\n      Re-evaluate C\u2085: ensure precision via multiple lag checks\n      Compute entropy: confirm piecewise structure\n\n  Forced restart rules:\n      Reinitialize if (grid_signatures/dimension > 3 and stuck)\n      Wall clock: min(time_per_grid, 20 seconds)\n\n  return (best_candidates[-1].tolist(), c5_bound, dimension)",
